// How Aerie turns a Lines model into an interactive diagram.
// Modules are grouped for explanation; this is a draft architecture description for review.
model aerie-flow: How Aerie works
  > One architecture model becomes an interactive picture for every audience.

audiences exec "Plain", manager "More detail" (default), engineer "Technical" (code)

author: Model author | Describes the system [person]
  > Writes the architecture once in a Lines file.

aerie: Aerie | One model, every audience [system]
  editor: Model editor | Write architecture as text [part]
    icon document
    > Loads a model or checks edits beside the diagram.
    @engineer: Live editor | src/app/live.ts

  meaning: Model tools | Check the model and its meaning [part]
    icon gear
    > Checks the text and resolves the parts, views and wording.
    @engineer: Language and semantics | src/lines and src/model
    lines: Lines language | Parse the text and report errors [module]
    semantics: Model semantics | Resolve views, wording and steps [module]

  picture: Diagram builder | Build an interactive picture [part]
    icon web
    > Places the diagram, draws it and responds to reader actions.
    @engineer: Layout, rendering and viewer | src/layout, src/render and src/app
    layout: Layout engine | Place boxes and connections [module]
    renderer: Signal renderer | Draw the diagram as SVG [module]
    viewer: Browser viewer | Open parts and follow flows [module]

reader: Diagram reader | Explore and understand [person]
  > Reads the diagram, changes wording, opens parts and follows scenarios.

author writes the model in editor
editor sends model text to semantics
semantics checks the text with lines
lines returns the parsed model to semantics
semantics supplies the resolved picture to layout
layout supplies positioned boxes to renderer
renderer supplies the drawing to viewer
viewer shows the diagram to reader

view big-picture: Big picture
  show author, aerie +1, reader
  scenario full-flow
  > Four stages explain how Aerie turns architecture text into a picture.

view inside: Inside Aerie
  show author, aerie +2, reader
  > The actual participants behind each high-level stage.

scenario full-flow: Create a diagram
  > How one model becomes an interactive picture, at a glance and step by step.
  author writes the model in editor
    > The author writes or edits a Lines file.
  editor sends model text to semantics
    > The live editor checks each change. If it finds errors, the last good diagram stays visible.
  semantics checks the text with lines
    > The language parses text into a canonical model and reports errors with their line and column.
  lines returns the parsed model to semantics
    > Model semantics resolves nesting, views, audience wording and scenarios.
  semantics supplies the resolved picture to layout
    > The viewer asks layout to place the resolved picture. Space is reserved for every audience.
  layout supplies positioned boxes to renderer
    > Signal uses the positions to draw SVG boxes, connections and labels.
  renderer supplies the drawing to viewer
    > The browser viewer displays the drawing and manages reader actions.
  viewer shows the diagram to reader
    > The reader explores the picture and can share a link to the same view and state.

  step 1: Write the model
    > Describe the system's parts and connections once in a Lines file.
  step 2-4: Check its meaning
    > The language checks the text; model semantics resolves the views and wording.
    @engineer: Parse and resolve the model
  step 5-7: Build the picture
    > Layout places the boxes and connections, then Signal draws the diagram.
    @engineer: Lay out and render SVG
  step 8: Explore the diagram
    > Readers open parts, change wording and follow flows on the same model.
